#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
The whole-world button, and 3D terrain on a round Earth.

- A small globe button sits under + and - beside the legend. It goes out to
  the whole world in the view you are in: the round globe at its opening
  size from the Globe view, the whole flat chart fitted to the window from
  the Flat map.
- 3D terrain is drawn on MapLibre's "globe": round at world scale, flattening
  only close up (from about zoom 11). The flat chart tilted at world scale,
  which stood on the screen like a slab on a column, is gone. Turning terrain
  off gives back whichever view was chosen.
- The map turns on every axis: right-drag (or Ctrl + drag on a Mac) turns and
  tilts it, Ctrl + right-drag rolls it, tilt goes to 85 degrees. The compass
  under the zoom buttons shows the tilt and turn; click it to stand the map
  back upright facing north.
- The sky over a tilted map is dark slate rather than MapLibre's bright blue.

Needs patch_list_0917.py applied first. Edits map/app.js, map/index.html and
map/test.mjs, anchored on exact text.

Run from the repo root:  python3 patch_world_terrain.py
"""
